 "The compass is a device with three principal pieces or parts - first; the outer box like, containing;...
The brass plate and glass cup at it. (It should be, the needle and card are contained). These; (I think, but, am wrong; no!)... are for holding down dust; or keeping things; out. Secondy;...
In one place (which seems, no) a pin in some; it goes... the pin in some. In second, some other in other some thing place. There... (No, that is in wrong...
No matter which place some... The... No!
...no, in first. Then (No no; it seems wrong)
There; are some thing (that thing). The glass.
And the needle.
There the brass and needle too...
But there some, which;...
This the compass!... So that there...
It works; and it, and I. A, that."
